  "term": "multivariate analysis of variance",
  "definition": "Multivariate analysis of variance is a statistical method used to test whether a group shows significant differences across several measured outcomes at the same time. In this study, a repeated-measures version was used to examine pre- to post-course changes in multiple self-reported skills together.",
